   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to creating a sustainable energy loan program in the town of Bedford",
    "basePrintNo": "S5762",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5762-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5762\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to creating a sustainable energy loan program in\nthe town of Bedford\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\nThis legislation is intended to reduce energy costs and greenhouse gas\nemissions as well as make energy efficiency and renewable energy\nimprovements more affordable to homeowners and businesses within the\ntown of Bedford. Accordingly, it authorizes the town of Bedford to\noffer sustainable energy loans to help homeowners and businesses\nwithin the town finance the installation of distributed generation\nrenewable energy sources (energy that is generated close to the point\nof use) and/or energy efficiency improvements.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the bill provides that it is the intent of the town of\nBedford to promote energy efficiency among its residents and\nbusinesses, including the promotion of energy efficiency improvements\nand the utilization of renewable energy sources in existing buildings\nwithin the town.\n\nSection 2 of the legislation provides definitions of \"distributed\ngeneration,\" \"renewable energy source\" and \"energy efficiency\nimprovement.\" It also authorizes the town of Bedford to offer, in its\ndiscretion, sustainable energy loans to help its homeowners and\nbusinesses finance the installation of distributed generation\nrenewable energy sources and/or energy efficiency improvements. The\nloans issued by the town under this program will be repaid by the\nborrower through an assessment levied by the town on the real property\nwhere the sustainable energy loan was applied. The total amount of\neach such loan provided by the town cannot exceed the actual cost of\nthe equipment and the materials necessary for the installation of\ndistributed generation renewable energy sources or the energy\nefficiency improvements.\n\nSection 2 provides further that the town of Bedford declares that this\nlegislation is necessary for the immediate protection of the public\ninterest and for the implementation of the energy efficiency and\ngreenhouse gas reduction plans of the town and the state of New York.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date, which is immediate.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nTo address the issue of global climate change and greenhouse gas\nemissions in the town of Bedford, the town has embarked on an effort\nto reduce energy demand from existing buildings to allow the town to\nmeet statewide energy efficiency goals. To assist residents and\nbusinesses within the town by making energy efficiency improvements\nmore affordable and to promote the installation and utilization of\nthese improvements, it is necessary to create a program to help\nfinance the cost of these energy efficiency improvements.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
