    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5762A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to creating a sustainable energy loan program in\nthe town of Bedford\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation seeks to reduce energy costs and greenhouse gas\nemissions as well as make energy efficiency and renewable energy\nimprovements more affordable to homeowners and businesses within the\ntown of Bedford.  Accordingly, it authorizes the town of Bedford to\noffer sustainable energy loans to help homeowners and businesses\nwithin the town finance the installation of distributed generation\nrenewable energy sources (energy that is generated close to the point\nof use) and/or energy efficiency improvements.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would establish that it is the intent of the\ntown of Bedford to promote energy efficiency among its residents and\nbusinesses, including the promotion of energy efficiency improvements\nand the utilization of renewable energy sources in existing buildings\nwithin the town.\n\nSection 2 of the legislation would establish definitions for\n\"distributed generation,\" \"renewable energy source\" and \"energy\nefficiency improvement\". It would also authorize the town of Bedford\nto offer, in its discretion, sustainable energy loans to help its\nhomeowners and businesses finance the installation of distributed\ngeneration renewable energy sources and/or energy efficiency\nimprovements.\n\nThis section would further authorize the town to use monies made\navailable for the program from federal grants to implement the\nsustainable energy loan program. he loans issued by the town under\nthis program will be repaid by the borrower through an assessment\nlevied by the town on the real property where the sustainable energy\nloan was applied. The total amount of each such loan provided by the\ntown cannot exceed the actual cost of the equipment and the materials\nnecessary for the installation of distributed generation renewable\nenergy sources or the energy efficiency improvements.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe town of Bedford has embarked on an effort to reduce energy demand\nfrom existing buildings to allow the town to meet statewide energy\nefficiency goals. To assist residents and businesses within the town\nby making energy efficiency improvements more affordable, and to\npromote the installation and utilization of these improvements, it is\nnecessary to create a program to help finance the cost of these energy\nefficiency improvements.\n\nThis bill seeks to achieve this goal.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone for State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
